  "releasedVersions": {
    "Switch": {"1":"Four fixed outputs, old typed scalar rules, numeric fallback; not executable in this slice", "2":"Dynamic legacy typed rules, output labels, scalar/date/regex comparisons; not executable in this slice", "3/3.1/3.2/3.3":"Modern filter rules with older filter-version/type-validation/default behavior; not executable in this slice", "3.4":"Latest rules/expression modes; filter version3"},
    "Merge": {"1":"Legacy append/key-match/key-remove/key-merge/index/multiplex/passThrough/wait; not executable in this slice", "2/2.1":"Two inputs, append/combinationMode fields/position/multiplex/chooseBranch waitForBoth; not executable in this slice", "3/3.1":"Multi-input append/position/chooseBranch, fields/all combinations, SQL; not executable in this slice", "3.2":"Latest modes, SQL empty-query result option added"}
  },
  "supported": {
    "Switch3.4":"Rules: and/or supported scalar/array/object comparisons from existing bounded native filter, first/all matches, none/extra/numeric fallback, output labels; expression mode: literal or whole-value $json integer output index, literal 1–100 numberOutputs. Explicit filter options required. Empty input returns one empty port like released module.",
    "Merge3.2":"Append and chooseBranch waitForAll with2–10 inputs; specifiedInput or empty item; combineByPosition with2–10 inputs; combineAll and combineByFields with exactly2 inputs. Deep/shallow preference/suffix/overrideEmpty clash handling. Field joins: five join modes, both/input1/input2 outputs, advanced field pairs including repeated destinations, dot-notation disabling, all/first match, bounded strict/fuzzy JSON comparisons. Exact tested helper outputs include nested array/object transitions and signed-zero retention.",
    "scheduler":"Single-run acyclic manual workflows containing Merge require at most one incoming edge per non-Merge node and per Merge input. A Merge must have all configured input ports connected to reachable nodes. Queue input batches with immediate item/input links; keep queues privately in persisted execution, defer Wait output routing until resume. No legacy forcing of otherwise inactive branches. Exact released enqueue helpers and waiting-input drain block are exercised separately; complete released scheduler is not run."
  },
  "unsupported":"Other released versions, date/regex filter operators, arbitrary JS/expressions, SQL/AlaSQL, providers/credentials, binary attachments, cycles/repeated loop generations, multiple incoming edges on the same input, custom error/retry policies, partial execution/editor/database/full scheduler parity.",
  "safety":"Existing2MiB documents,1MiB values,8MiB state,10,000 items,100,000 structural entries,40 depth,500 steps,120s active-time and60s Wait caps remain. Switch aggregate fan-out capped before each clone at10,000 items/8MiB and1,000,000 condition evaluations; Merge Cartesian/field/iteration work capped before allocation at10,000 outputs/1,000,000 work units with cancellation/deadline checks. Recursive literal dangerous Merge own keys and non-index array output properties are deliberate rejections. Exact equality, error-presence equality, dangerous-key deviations and JSON-representation deviations are recorded separately.",
  "sourceInventory":"source-option-inventory.json:118 static released parameter definitions; dynamic spreads/filter generated schemas excluded explicitly",
  "ui":"Candidate editor supports Switch/Merge creation, source-output/target-input selection and exact connection removal; actual isolated stage browser evidence in ui-observations.json. Production host and original editor not validated."
